  "synopsisContentVersion": "1.0.0",
  "introduction": "England's civil war has brought the rival houses of Lancaster and York into Parliament itself. Henry VI hopes that a compromise over the succession can preserve peace, but his queen refuses to sacrifice their son's inheritance, while York's sons urge their father to seize the crown immediately. Battles, family vengeance, diplomatic marriages, and abrupt changes of allegiance turn kings into prisoners and prisoners into kings. Amid the struggle, Richard of Gloucester begins to imagine a power greater than any loyalty to his brothers.",
  "fullSynopsis": [
    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-summary-01",
      "text": "After a Yorkist victory, the Duke of York occupies Henry VI's throne in Parliament. To avoid further bloodshed and keep the crown during his lifetime, Henry agrees that York and his heirs will succeed him, disinheriting Prince Edward. Margaret rejects this settlement and takes the prince to join her northern supporters. York's sons meanwhile persuade him that his oath need not prevent an immediate bid for kingship. Before he can gather sufficient strength, Margaret's army approaches Sandal Castle. York chooses battle despite being outnumbered.",
