    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-summary-02",
      "text": "Clifford murders York's young son Rutland in revenge for his own father's death. Captured after defeat, York is tormented with a paper crown and a cloth stained with Rutland's blood. Margaret and Clifford stab him, and she orders his head displayed at York. Edward and Richard learn what has happened and renew the struggle with Warwick. After bitter challenges and an uncertain battle at Towton, the Yorkists prevail. Henry, driven from the fighting, witnesses a son who has killed his father and a father who has killed his son: the civil war has spread the ruling families' violence through ordinary households. Clifford dies of his wounds; the victors order his head to replace York's.",
