    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-summary-03",
      "text": "Edward becomes king and sends Warwick to seek a French marriage with Lady Bona. Henry, returning secretly from Scotland, is captured and sent to the Tower. At home Edward pressures the widowed Lady Grey to exchange sexual favors for restoration of her husband's lands. When she refuses, he resolves to marry her. Richard privately declares his own ambition for the crown, accepting deception and murder as means of overcoming the relatives who stand in his way.",
