    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-summary-04",
      "text": "In France, Warwick nearly secures Bona for Edward, frustrating Margaret's appeal for aid. News that Edward has already married Lady Grey transforms the negotiation. Humiliated, Warwick abandons Edward and joins Margaret; the French king promises troops, and Prince Edward pledges himself to Warwick's daughter. Clarence also deserts his brother, seeking Warwick's other daughter. Warwick's forces surprise Edward in his camp and take him prisoner. The pregnant Queen Elizabeth seeks sanctuary, while Richard and Hastings arrange Edward's escape during a hunting excursion.",
