    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-summary-06",
      "text": "The Yorkists defeat Margaret at Tewkesbury. Edward orders Somerset's execution and Oxford's imprisonment. When the captive Prince Edward defies his conquerors, Edward, Richard, and Clarence stab him before his mother. Richard then goes to the Tower and murders Henry, cutting short the former king's prophecy of the suffering he will cause. Richard plans to turn Edward against Clarence and clear his own path to power. Edward celebrates his recovered throne, his infant son, and what he believes are his brothers' love and the country's peace. Margaret is to be ransomed to France. Richard's affectionate kiss for the baby conceals a threat to the family whose security Edward proclaims.",
