  "acts": [
    {
      "act": 1,
      "sectionId": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-act-4842",
      "label": "ACT I",
      "summary": "York takes Henry's throne in Parliament, backed by Warwick and armed supporters. Henry keeps the crown for life by naming York's line as successors, thereby disinheriting his own son. Margaret refuses to accept the bargain and leaves with Prince Edward to fight for his rights. At Sandal, Richard and Edward persuade York to pursue the crown at once despite his oath. Margaret's army arrives before he is ready, but he chooses to meet its superior numbers. Clifford kills the helpless Rutland to avenge his father. Defeated and captured, York is mocked with a paper crown and Rutland's bloodstained cloth. Clifford and Margaret stab him; she orders his head set above York's gates.",
