    {
      "act": 3,
      "sectionId": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth-act-86729",
      "label": "ACT III",
      "summary": "Two keepers capture Henry after his secret return from Scotland. He submits while questioning the shifting allegiance that makes them Edward's subjects rather than his. Edward attempts to buy Lady Grey's sexual compliance with the restoration of her children's lands, but her refusal leads him to propose marriage. Henry is sent to the Tower. Left alone, Richard resolves to pursue the crown through calculated deceit and violence. In France, Warwick's embassy appears to secure Bona's marriage and defeat Margaret's hopes of military aid. Letters announcing Edward's marriage to Lady Grey reverse that outcome. Warwick renounces Edward, joins Margaret out of wounded honor, and secures the promise of French troops. Prince Edward promises to marry Warwick's daughter as a pledge of the new alliance.",
