      "label": "ACT V",
      "summary": "At Coventry Clarence breaks with Warwick and returns to Edward, invoking loyalty to his father's house. Edward wins at Barnet; Warwick dies after hearing that Montague has also fallen. Margaret, newly arrived from France, urges her remaining commanders to fight on, but they are defeated at Tewkesbury. Edward sentences Somerset to death and Oxford to imprisonment. The captive Prince Edward refuses submission, and all three Yorkist brothers stab him. Richard hurries to the Tower, murders Henry, and announces his intention to remove Clarence next by manipulating Edward's fears. Back at court, Edward celebrates the infant Prince Edward and imagines his dynasty secure. Richard kisses the child while privately revealing hostility. Margaret's ransom is reported, and Edward orders her sent to France before calling for festivities.",
